WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
(crowd cheers enthusiastically)

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:01.666
- All right, it's almost time to go

00:00:01.666 --> 00:00:03.330
but I want to leave
you with one last story

00:00:03.330 --> 00:00:04.410
to lift your spirits!

00:00:04.410 --> 00:00:05.739
This is what I'm liking:

00:00:05.739 --> 00:00:08.490
(jovial jingle)

00:00:08.490 --> 00:00:11.310
Let me introduce you to Braxton.

00:00:11.310 --> 00:00:14.160
At 20 years old, he just
became our country's

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:15.420
youngest lawyer.

00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:17.940
He's already lived an extraordinary life.

00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:20.730
At 10, he was taking college courses.

00:00:20.730 --> 00:00:22.080
Through middle and high school,

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:24.240
he was also working toward his Bachelor's

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:26.480
at Harvard, so we were on a similar track.

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:27.480
(audience laughs)

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:29.580
In fact, he's the only student

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:31.230
in the university's history

00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:35.109
to graduate high school
and Harvard simultaneously.

00:00:35.109 --> 00:00:36.480
(audience applauds and cheers)

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:37.320
What??

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:39.270
He went on to graduate law school

00:00:39.270 --> 00:00:41.280
two years later, and earlier this year

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:43.530
he passed the Bar, no big deal,

00:00:43.530 --> 00:00:45.240
we have Braxton on the line right now

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:47.613
watching from KSNW Wichita.

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:51.000
What's up Braxton?

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:51.990
- Hi, how are you?

00:00:51.990 --> 00:00:54.660
- I'm not as awesome as you, but like

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:56.490
you're- congratulations!

00:00:56.490 --> 00:00:57.990
You're just extraordinary!

00:00:57.990 --> 00:01:00.150
So where were you when you found out

00:01:00.150 --> 00:01:01.980
that you passed the Bar?

00:01:01.980 --> 00:01:04.593
- So, we'd actually just
entered a movie theater.

00:01:05.970 --> 00:01:07.440
Scrolling through social media,

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:09.810
saw one of my friends got their scores,

00:01:09.810 --> 00:01:11.640
figured my score's probably in as well,

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:13.080
started to panic,

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:15.870
found out I passed, my
parents were ecstatic,

00:01:15.870 --> 00:01:17.370
and we saw the movie.

00:01:17.370 --> 00:01:18.203
- And we saw-

00:01:18.203 --> 00:01:19.509
and we watched the movie!

00:01:19.509 --> 00:01:20.400
(laughs incredulously)

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:21.233
I love it!

00:01:21.233 --> 00:01:22.144
I love-

00:01:22.144 --> 00:01:22.977
you're casual-

00:01:22.977 --> 00:01:23.810
(stutters)

00:01:23.810 --> 00:01:26.070
you moved your cat like, so effortlessly,

00:01:26.070 --> 00:01:27.660
that was nice work.

00:01:27.660 --> 00:01:29.550
So are you working yet?

00:01:29.550 --> 00:01:30.990
- I haven't decided on a law firm

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:32.220
or anything yet.

00:01:32.220 --> 00:01:33.930
I had an externship with the local

00:01:33.930 --> 00:01:36.480
county/city attorney.

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:37.800
You have to kind of be more than one thing

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:39.870
out here 'cause it's so desolate.

00:01:39.870 --> 00:01:40.950
You know, tried a few people

00:01:40.950 --> 00:01:42.810
for traffic infractions,

00:01:42.810 --> 00:01:43.643
I got 'em.

00:01:43.643 --> 00:01:44.490
I mean, they were on camera,

00:01:44.490 --> 00:01:46.400
but that's beside the
point, I still got 'em.

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:47.233
(Kelly and audience chuckle)

00:01:47.233 --> 00:01:49.029
And I'm keepin' our city safer.

00:01:49.029 --> 00:01:49.862
(Kelly laughs)

00:01:49.862 --> 00:01:51.540
That's my interest; trials, litigation,

00:01:51.540 --> 00:01:52.680
that sort of thing.

00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:53.513
- Oh my God.

00:01:53.513 --> 00:01:55.560
You are, you're such an amazing young man.

00:01:55.560 --> 00:01:57.090
Thank you so much Braxton

00:01:57.090 --> 00:01:58.389
and congratulations again.

00:01:58.389 --> 00:01:59.700
(audience cheers enthusiastically)

00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:02.389
I'm liking your post right now.

00:02:02.389 --> 00:02:03.780
(bell dings)

00:02:03.780 --> 00:02:04.650
And that's not all.

00:02:04.650 --> 00:02:06.330
Our season-long partner, Pilot Pen,

00:02:06.330 --> 00:02:07.830
makers of G-2, the go to pen of

00:02:07.830 --> 00:02:08.730
the Kelly Clarkson Show,

00:02:08.730 --> 00:02:10.830
want to honor ultimate overachievers

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:12.030
just like you sir, so they're-

00:02:12.030 --> 00:02:14.430
I don't know if anyone
is like you, but sure.

00:02:14.430 --> 00:02:15.720
So they're gonna be writing you a check

00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:17.251
for $1,000 , how's that sound?

00:02:17.251 --> 00:02:18.379
(audience cheers and applauds)

00:02:18.379 --> 00:02:20.491
(Kelly giggles)

00:02:20.491 --> 00:02:21.324
- Thank you.

00:02:21.324 --> 00:02:22.890
- [Kelly] Oh my gosh, good luck in life!

00:02:22.890 --> 00:02:24.630
You are super blessed, man!

00:02:24.630 --> 00:02:25.593
Hard worker!

